   "text": "The drawing shows the sodium salt of desferrithiocin, a 4-methyl-4,5-dihydrothiazole-4-carboxylate carrying a 3-hydroxypyridin-2-yl group at C2.\n\n- **Thiazoline ring:** the ring runs S\u2013CH2\u2013C(quaternary)\u2013N=C. The C=N double bond is between N and the carbon attached to the pyridine.\n- **Quaternary carbon:** it bears the carboxylate (C(=O)[O\u207b]), a methyl on a wedge bond, the ring CH2 and the ring N.\n- **Pyridine ring:** it is attached through C2, its ring N is adjacent to that carbon, and the OH sits on the next carbon (C3).\n- **Counter-ion:** Na\u207a.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** the methyl is on a wedge, pointing toward the viewer. The other three substituents then run N (upper right), COO\u207b (upper left) and CH2 (down). Seen from the methyl side, N \u2192 COO\u207b \u2192 CH2 goes counterclockwise, which gives `@` for the neighbour order in the SMILES below.\n\nAs a check, the CIP priorities are N > CH2S > COO\u207b > CH3. With the methyl toward the viewer, N \u2192 CH2S \u2192 COO\u207b appears clockwise, so reversing it gives S, which matches the known (S)-desferrithiocin.\n\nSMILES: [Na+].C[C@]1(C(=O)[O-])CSC(=N1)c1ncccc1O"
